	"documentation": {
		"summary": "Escher's Impossible Objects \u2014 a clockwise ascending loop",
		"layout": "A perimeter loop that ascends clockwise: north side height-1, east side height-2, south side height-3, west side height-4. Each step up feels locally valid \u2014 you're just climbing stairs. But when you complete the loop, you're impossibly back where you started at height-1. The center is a void or sunken area. Artifacts placed along the loop path. The spatial paradox IS the lesson: local coherence, global impossibility.",
		"spatial_pattern": "ascending_loop",
		"key_elements": [
			"Clockwise ascending perimeter: 1 \u2192 2 \u2192 3 \u2192 4 \u2192 back to 1",
			"Each side feels like a natural step up",
			"Completing the loop reveals the impossibility",
			"Central void \u2014 no shortcut through the paradox",
			"Escher staircase, Penrose triangle, Magritte pipe along the path"
		]
	},
